TEXT 0 -224 Left 2 ;Second-order high-pass (series RLC, output on L): H(s) = s² / (s² + s ω0/Q + ω0²)\nω0 = 1/√(LC) = 31.6 krad/s (f0 ≈ 5.03 kHz) and Q = √(L/C) / R ≈ 2.1: two complex poles at −ω0/2Q ± jω0√(1 − 1/4Q²). A double zero at s = 0.\nStep: out jumps to 1, rings and decays to 0. Bode: +40 dB/decade below f0, a peak near f0 and flat above; the phase goes from +180° to 0.
